Basic relationship:
Derivation rules cannot be applied to both piecewise definitions.
f(x)={x^2: x>0, x^3+x^4: x<=0}
f'(0) = lim{h->0, (g(h)-g(0))/h}, lim{x->0+, (h^2-0)/h} = 0, lim{x->0-, (h^3+h^4-0)/h} = 0

+ Assymptotes:
Vertical assymptotes (out of domain): {k=0, n, {lim x->A[k], f(x)}, {lim x->A[k]+, f(x)}, {lim x->A[k]-, f(x)}}
Horizontal assymptotes: {lim x->\inf, f(x)}, {lim x->-\inf, f(x)}
Oblique assymptotes: {lim x->A[k], f(x)}=g(x), (k={lim x->A[k], f(x)/x}, b={lim x->A[k], f(x)-kx}, -> y=kx+b)
